 difficulty_explanation = """
 Participants build the application from six focused notes and /assets/seed_data.json; no starter implementation or saved snippets are supplied. Difficulty is concentrated in supported-source execution and durable library state. Fresh isolated runs must cancel old work, preserve the last completed preview after synchronous or asynchronous failure, report user-source lines, and stop supported literal loops and callbacks within the shared five-second budget. Unsupported dynamic execution is refused; the task does not promise interruption of arbitrary browser-native time bombs.
 
-The saved library preserves stable identities, exact title/filename/source and revisions. A stale editor cannot overwrite or delete newer work, rejected title collisions and invalid filenames are atomic, duplicates remain independent, and deleted identities cannot be recreated by stale updates. Each mutation chain uses dedicated records and meaningful positive controls. Final persistence establishes its own records before one actual restart and verifies both durability and continued revision-aware saving.
